Commit:     Dennis Dyall Wallin <dennis@dyallo.se>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 17:11:49 2026 +0200

    fix(core): remove RandomNumberGeneratorExt in favour of the runtime API (YESDK-1633, 25c)
    
    GetInt32 ported the runtime's rejection sampler with the loop
    condition inverted for ranges of 2^31 or wider: `uint result =
    int.MaxValue; while (result > range)` never entered, so
    GetInt32(int.MinValue, int.MaxValue) returned -1 every time without
    drawing any random bytes. Both exception messages were also garbled
    string literals.
    
    The type had no callers in the SDK; GetByte and Fill only existed to
    serve each other. Delete it and its unshipped PublicAPI entries.
    RandomNumberGenerator.GetInt32, RandomNumberGenerator.Fill and
    rng.GetBytes(Span<byte>) cover every use.
    
    The YESDK-1633 wide-range repro and its counting RNG helper go with
    the type they tested.

